					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1118714#post-3795368</guid>
				<title>+100</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1118714/excerpts-from-the-medical-tragedy-of-dr-bartholomew-artz-aut#post-3795368</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 09 May 2018 20:48:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Ihp</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1267048</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p><strong>The Doctor</strong></p> <p>What merry sight is this?<br /> A century pass'd since my creation!</p> <p><strong>Pocks</strong><br /> Indeed, good doctor.<br /> It seems our presentation was most effective.<br /> Come, shall we take a bow?</p> <p><strong>The Doctor</strong><br /> Nay, an archer cannot help.<br /> My work must be done alone.<br /> The pestilence still exists,<br /> And my work must continue anon.</p> <p><strong>Pocks</strong><br /> Come, then.<br /> Unto the way between worlds,<br /> Where your cure shall be spread.</p> <p><em>Exit The Doctor, Pocks, and Abominations several</em>.</p> <hr /> <p>In all seriousness, I have to thank my Shakespeare professor, Dr. Simon Morgan-Russel, for inspiring me to write this and teaching Shakespearean language so damn well that I managed to get through this with some help from Kestin/River.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
