						 <p>Don't know how fair it would be for me to upvote this given that I had more than a stray line's hand in it, so +0 for safety, but now that I've read it fully, I must admire the Shakespeareanishness of it all once again. I've read enough of his work to feel I know his style, and this really does evoke him quite well in my opinion. (The &quot;craving&quot; joke in particular is so like him. XD)</p> 
