				<wikidot:authorName>Aurabek</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1649410</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I once wrote several scenes (each including songs) of &quot;Hamlet of Penzance&quot; for a class. Had the rest of it outlined, too. The only things really missing were a few of the songs, as the dialogue is easy when you are just copying Shakespeare by way of Gilbert and Sullivan. I would have finished it if I didn't have the rug ripped out from under me and the performance cancelled. Given that you seem to be a much better writer (all due credit to Kestin as well- Iambic Pentameter isn't easy!) than I, I have faith in you being able to finish! An audio version might be an intermediate step before calling Kenneth Branagh, and it might be fun to boot. Heck, for whatever the word of an internet stranger is worth, I'll help!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
